  "discussion": {
    "headline": "dangerous heat, humidity with multiple rounds of storms late this week",
    "dateLine": "2:00 p.m. Tuesday, June 9, 2026",
    "excerpt": "The second week of June kicked off on a mostly cloudy, cooler and less humid note across northern MD, southeastern PA and the Lower Susquehanna Valley, and today has turned out to be quite similar. Moist, southeasterly flow off the Atlantic caused a relatively narrow band of low clouds to develop along the eastern slopes of the Appalachians from northern PA through the Delmarva Region on Monday, and those clouds hung tough this morning. …",
